     [38;5;246mTasks carry a due date; you get alerted as it approaches and when it passes. The only trigger that's genuinely [39m
     [38;5;246museful when you're the sole editor. Needs due dates in the task model.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Explicit reminders
     [38;5;246mYou set a reminder time on a task independently of its due date ('poke me Thursday at 9'). More control, slightly [39m
     [38;5;246mmore UI.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Change log, not notifications
     [38;5;246mNo alerts — just an activity history of what changed and when. Useful for recall, zero timing/permission [39m
     [38;5;246mcomplexity.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Reconsider multi-user
     [38;5;246mThe feature you actually wanted requires other people. Revisit the single-user decision before going further.[39m
